🏏 Hand Cricket Game — C++

A simple console-based Hand Cricket Game developed in C++ using the Dev-C++ IDE.

The game follows basic hand-cricket rules where the player and computer select numbers from 1 to 6. If both numbers are the same, the batter is considered OUT. Otherwise, the selected batting number is added to the batter's score.

The project is designed for beginners and demonstrates the use of functions, loops, conditional statements, random number generation, input validation, and basic game logic.

🎮 Game Features
🏏 Console-based hand cricket gameplay
🎲 Random number generation from 1 to 6
⌨️ Player input restricted to 1–6
❌ Invalid inputs are rejected and the ball is replayed
💬 Ball-by-ball commentary
🪙 Head/Tails toss before the match
👤 Player can choose:
