🧱 Recommended Coding Practices

The project should follow basic C++ coding conventions.

Meaningful Names

Use descriptive names such as:

playerScore
computerScore
playerChoice
computerChoice
totalOvers
totalWickets
currentOver
currentBall


Avoid unclear names such as:

x
a
b
n
temp1

Constants

Important fixed values can be represented using constants:

const int MIN_NUMBER = 1;
const int MAX_NUMBER = 6;
const int BALLS_PER_OVER = 6;


This makes the program easier to understand and modify.

Functions

Separate major tasks into functions.

For example:

getValidInput()


can handle player input validation, while:

generateRandomNumber()


can handle random number generation.

📝 Comments

Comments should be used to explain the purpose of important sections of the program.

Example:

// Generate a random number between 1 and 6
int generateRandomNumber()
{
    return rand() % 6 + 1;
}


Another example:

// Check whether the batter is out.
// In hand cricket, matching numbers mean dismissal.
if (playerChoice == computerChoice)
{
    wickets++;
}


Comments should explain why something is being done rather than unnecessarily describing every individual line.

